## Highlights
A composite comprising $\mathrm{NiCo}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{4}$ spinel and CoO nanoparticles embedded within carbon nanotubes derived from a bimetallic NiCo-MOF at $700~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ under $\mathbf{N}_{2}$ atmosphere; HIV-1 probe DNA immobilized onto the NiCo2O4/CoO@CNTs composite; NiCo2O4/CoO@CNT-based bioassay displayed superior sensing performances.
